    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass and the full build succeeds. Here's a summary of what I changed to satisfy the specification.\n\n## What changed\n\n**`householdId` is now deterministic and always assigned**\n- `Household.java` \u2014 rekeyed the household from `(lastName, address)` to `(lastName, postcode)` and made `id()` return the **first 12 hex chars of SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)**. Removed the now-unused `same()` helper.\n- `AssignOwnerHousehold.java` \u2014 stamps that deterministic id onto **every** owner unconditionally. No more `sharesHousehold` gate and no more backfilling existing members (a deterministic id needs no coordination), so the class shrank to one responsibility and no longer needs the repository or request DTO.\n\n**`sharesHousehold` now only bypasses the duplicate block**\n- `EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity.java` \u2014 became a household-duplicate guard: it derives the request's household id and rejects with **409** when an existing owner already belongs to that household, *unless* `sharesHousehold=true`, in which case it returns early (declared member). The old telephone+email+household key check was subsumed by this rule, so it's gone.\n\n**A declared member is not a suspected duplicate**\n- `AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java` \u2014 now also reads the request DTO and short-circuits (never flags) when `sharesHousehold=true`.\n\n**Household-size input keys off the computed id**\n- `AssignOwnerHouseholdSize.java` \u2014 since `householdId` is always present now, the dead null-guard was removed; it counts existing members sharing the computed id plus the new owner.\n\n**Docs kept in sync** \u2014 updated the pipeline YAML step comments, the two escalation-class javadocs, and the OpenAPI descriptions for `householdId`, `sharesHousehold`, and `possibleDuplicate`.\n\n## Verification\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId` passes: same lastName+postcode \u2192 same `householdId` (the second one via `sharesHousehold` bypassing the 409), different lastName \u2192 different `householdId`.\n- Full `./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 test run, 0 failures.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: the spec redefines the create endpoint's single duplicate block to be household-keyed, so the previous exact telephone/email duplicate detection is now folded into (and subsumed by) the household check rather than kept as a separate cross-household check. The `identityKey` field is still computed and exposed on the response (via `OwnerIdentity`), now using the deterministic household id.",
